      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The park was originally a private garden of the Ming Dynasty before the French Concession reopened it in 1909.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.chinahighlights.com/shanghai/attraction/fuxing-park.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 2007 a comprehensive renovation preserved its historic character, reinforcing the park's distinctive French garden atmosphere.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://english.shanghai.gov.cn/en-Parks/20250220/636b3df5761e4055b731a92d2abddcb3.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 6.4‑meter, 70‑ton statue of Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels stands in the northern part of Fuxing Park, erected in 1985 to mark Engels' 90th death anniversary.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
